    "body": "### Contact Details (e.g. Tox ID or email)\n\nnulflox@disroot.org\n\n### qTox Version\n\n1.17.6\n\n### Commit Hash\n\n54345d1085628950af4176e6b4873513db0de4f3\n\n### Toxcore Version\n\n0.2.13\n\n### Qt Version\n\n5.12.12\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Start an another Tox client (private Skymu branch in this case, that locks .tox file on login)\n2. Login with the another client\n3. Start qTox\n4. Try to login\n\n### Observed Behavior\n\n<img width=\"424\" height=\"307\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5bb4197d-a1a6-44ae-8d0b-e7f156a676e3\" />\n\nThe name after the Skype trademark is the profile name.\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nSomething that's not straight up incorrect. \"An error occurred\", \"File is locked\", etc.\n\n### Reproducibility\n\nAlways\n\n### Operating System\n\nWindows\n\n### Operating System version/distro/name/etc.\n\nWindows 10 (Enterprise LTSC, 21H2, 19044.7058)\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\n[15:59:47.680 UTC] persistence/profile.cpp:146 : Debug: Loading tox save  \"C:/Users/EggToast/AppData/Roaming/tox\\\\eggkymu.tox\"\n[15:59:47.680 UTC] persistence/profile.cpp:154 : Critical: The tox save file  \"C:/Users/EggToast/AppData/Roaming/tox\\\\eggkymu.tox\"  couldn't' be opened\n```",
